WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.618 --> 00:00:03.490
(rocket blast)

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.400
- What's up Believe Nation.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.233
It's Evan.

00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:07.771
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:09.689
more than they believe in themselves

00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:12.873
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in you,

00:00:12.873 --> 00:00:16.364
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:18.040
I started the MentorMe
series with the goal

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.162
to try to learn from people
who've done a lot more than us,

00:00:20.162 --> 00:00:22.606
try to hang out with people
who've had more success

00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:24.836
than us and hopefully
some of their beliefs,

00:00:24.836 --> 00:00:27.331
some of their mindset, some
of their way of working

00:00:27.331 --> 00:00:28.917
seeps into us to help us become

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.546
the best version of ourselves.

00:00:31.546 --> 00:00:33.333
So today we're going to
learn from Will Smith

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.914
and his work ethic.

00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:36.038
Mentor me, Will.

00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:38.071
Remember three is my personal favorite,

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.412
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:42.184
Also, as your watching,
if you hear something

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:43.712
that really resonates with you,

00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:45.063
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:45.063 --> 00:00:46.251
and put quotes around it, so other people

00:00:46.251 --> 00:00:48.354
can be inspired by it as well,

00:00:48.354 --> 00:00:50.053
and if you leave it within
the first couple of hours

00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:51.983
of this video going live,
you have a chance to win

00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:54.212
one of two daily prizes.

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:56.962
(dramatic music)

00:01:07.215 --> 00:01:10.185
- I think that you are so
incredible in all areas,

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:11.724
and you are so talented

00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:13.771
in so many ways, obviously.
- Thank you, thank you.

00:01:13.771 --> 00:01:16.363
- But you seem to have always been this.

00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:19.285
I mean, obviously we grow
and we get better and better,

00:01:19.285 --> 00:01:21.610
but what was the driving force?

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.566
Have you always been on some
kind of quest to be better.

00:01:24.566 --> 00:01:26.992
- You know there was, excuse me,

00:01:26.992 --> 00:01:31.159
there was a moment when I
was about nine years old,

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.331
and I was at the
Resurrection Baptist Church.

00:01:35.331 --> 00:01:37.221
That was the church I went to growing up,

00:01:37.221 --> 00:01:39.646
and my grandmother was
always in charge of all

00:01:39.646 --> 00:01:42.896
of the recitals and Easter recitations,

00:01:43.902 --> 00:01:47.702
and all of that stuff,
so I was playing a piano,

00:01:47.702 --> 00:01:52.003
and I remember my grandmother
was standing back off-stage,

00:01:52.003 --> 00:01:54.510
and she put me last in
the show and everything

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.620
and I had learned Für Elise
and I was playin' Für Elise,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.585
and I'm goin' and goin' and
goin' and I never learned

00:02:01.585 --> 00:02:02.807
how to end it, right.

00:02:02.807 --> 00:02:03.872
(laughter)

00:02:03.872 --> 00:02:05.549
So I was just playin'
and playin' and playin'

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:07.374
and my grandmother was standin' backstage

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:10.973
and I was lookin' and
playin' and that look

00:02:10.973 --> 00:02:15.056
of pride and happiness,
on my grandmother's face,

00:02:18.141 --> 00:02:19.965
that's my life force.

00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:24.019
Everything I do, I just
need that look, you know,

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:25.026
in my wife's eyes,

00:02:25.026 --> 00:02:25.859
(applause)

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:26.698
in my daughter's eyes.

00:02:26.698 --> 00:02:28.575
(cheering and applause)

00:02:28.575 --> 00:02:33.470
It's just, you know, I
realized very, very young,

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.717
that there's no easy way around it.

00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:39.140
No matter how talented you are,

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.968
your talent is going to fail
you if you're not skilled.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.268
You know, if you don't study,
if you don't work really hard

00:02:45.268 --> 00:02:48.843
and dedicate yourself to
being better every single day,

00:02:48.843 --> 00:02:51.926
you'll never be able to
communicate with people

00:02:51.926 --> 00:02:53.734
with your artistry the way that you want.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:57.621
So it's that moment, I just
remembered so distinctly

00:02:57.621 --> 00:03:00.217
and how good it felt,
an I just, I need it!

00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:01.050
(laughs)

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:01.883
- Yeah.

00:03:01.883 --> 00:03:05.232
- I believe and I learned very young --

00:03:05.232 --> 00:03:06.065
- [Charlie] From parents.

00:03:06.065 --> 00:03:09.651
- From my parents,
absolutely, that you don't

00:03:09.651 --> 00:03:11.750
try to build a wall.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.649
You don't set out to build a wall.

00:03:13.649 --> 00:03:16.676
You don't say, "I'm going to
build the biggest, baddest,

00:03:16.676 --> 00:03:19.406
greatest wall that's ever been built."

00:03:19.406 --> 00:03:20.365
You don't start there.

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:23.516
You say, "I'm going to lay this brick--"

00:03:23.516 --> 00:03:24.349
- Yeah.

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:27.530
- "As perfectly as a brick can be laid.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.397
"There will not be one brick
on the face of the earth,

00:03:29.397 --> 00:03:30.846
"that's going to be laid
better than this brick

00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:33.548
"that I'm going to lay
in this next 10 minutes."

00:03:33.548 --> 00:03:36.210
and you do that every single day--

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.054
- [Charlie] And soon you have a wall.

00:03:37.054 --> 00:03:38.369
- And soon you have a wall.

00:03:38.369 --> 00:03:42.114
And I think psychologically,
the advantage that,

00:03:42.114 --> 00:03:46.350
that gives me over a lot
of people that I have

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.825
been in competition with
in different situations,

00:03:48.825 --> 00:03:51.564
is it's difficult to take the first step

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:52.975
when you look how big--

00:03:52.975 --> 00:03:54.835
- Yeah.
- The task is.

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:56.704
- The task is never huge to me.

00:03:56.704 --> 00:03:58.497
It's always one brick.
- Yeah, me too.

00:03:58.497 --> 00:03:59.330
- Me too.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:03.497
- There's a concept that,
I don't want to be an icon.

00:04:08.505 --> 00:04:10.615
I want to be an idea.

00:04:10.615 --> 00:04:13.437
You know, I want to represent an idea.

00:04:13.437 --> 00:04:16.104
I want to represent possibilities.

00:04:17.476 --> 00:04:20.059
I want to represent magic, right,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.187
that you're in a universe
and two plus two equals four.

00:04:26.087 --> 00:04:28.096
Two plus two only equals
four if you accept

00:04:28.096 --> 00:04:30.610
that two plus two equals four.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.235
Two plus two's going to
be what I want it to be.

00:04:33.235 --> 00:04:36.568
You know, and there's a redemptive power

00:04:40.709 --> 00:04:42.792
that making a choice has.

00:04:44.621 --> 00:04:47.959
Rather than feeling like you're at affect

00:04:47.959 --> 00:04:51.057
to all the things that are happening.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.319
Make a choice, right.

00:04:53.319 --> 00:04:56.362
You just decide what it's going to be,

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.654
who you're going to be,
how, you're going to do it.

00:04:58.654 --> 00:05:02.459
Just decide and then from that point,

00:05:02.459 --> 00:05:04.164
the universe is gon' get out your way.

00:05:04.164 --> 00:05:06.601
It's water, it wants to move

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.933
and go around stuff.
- Yeah.

00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:11.683
- So for me, I want to
represent possibilities.

00:05:13.429 --> 00:05:18.334
I want to represent the idea
that you really can make

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.167
what you want.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:22.556
One of my favorite books is The Alchemist.

00:05:22.556 --> 00:05:24.007
Paulo Coelho.

00:05:24.007 --> 00:05:26.007
And I just believe that.

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:32.250
I believe that I can create
whatever I want to create.

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:37.088
If I can put my head
on it right, study it,

00:05:37.088 --> 00:05:40.671
learn the patterns and,
you know, it's hard

00:05:41.527 --> 00:05:45.176
to put into words, real
metaphysical, esoteric nonsense,

00:05:45.176 --> 00:05:49.936
but I feel very strongly that
we are who we choose to be.

00:05:49.936 --> 00:05:54.103
The only thing that I see,
that is distinctly different

00:05:56.308 --> 00:06:00.475
about me, is I'm not afraid
to die on a treadmill.

00:06:01.996 --> 00:06:03.890
Right, I will run--

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:04.723
- You will not be outworked.

00:06:04.723 --> 00:06:07.048
- I will not be outworked!
- Right.

00:06:07.048 --> 00:06:09.183
- Period, you know.
- Yeah.

00:06:09.183 --> 00:06:12.099
- You might have more talent than me.

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:14.017
You might be smarter than me.

00:06:14.017 --> 00:06:16.335
You might be sexier than me.

00:06:16.335 --> 00:06:18.274
You might be all of those things.

00:06:18.274 --> 00:06:21.243
You got it on me in nine categories.

00:06:21.243 --> 00:06:23.306
But if we get on the treadmill, together.

00:06:23.306 --> 00:06:24.139
(Tavis laughs)

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:24.972
Right.

00:06:24.972 --> 00:06:25.805
There's two things.

00:06:25.805 --> 00:06:26.642
You're gettin' off first--

00:06:26.642 --> 00:06:27.475
- Yeah.

00:06:27.475 --> 00:06:29.435
- Or I'm going to die.

00:06:29.435 --> 00:06:31.991
It's really that simple, right!

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.319
So, let's go back to the
question about what if people

00:06:35.319 --> 00:06:36.152
block me out?

00:06:36.152 --> 00:06:37.128
It's going to be two options.

00:06:37.128 --> 00:06:37.961
- Yeah.

00:06:37.961 --> 00:06:40.832
- I'm going to get back in,
or I'm going to be dead.

00:06:40.832 --> 00:06:41.665
- Yeah.

00:06:41.665 --> 00:06:42.498
- Right (laughs).

00:06:42.498 --> 00:06:44.945
It's like, you're not going to outwork me.

00:06:44.945 --> 00:06:48.862
It's a very, it's such
a simple, basic concept,

00:06:49.996 --> 00:06:53.663
is the guy who is willing
to hustle the most

00:06:57.935 --> 00:07:00.654
is going to be the guy that
just gets that loose ball.

00:07:00.654 --> 00:07:03.581
You know, it's oh, and he
got the oh, okay he got two.

00:07:03.581 --> 00:07:05.773
Whew, he's hustling, he grabbed that one.

00:07:05.773 --> 00:07:08.792
It was going to be out of
bounds, but he saved it back in.

00:07:08.792 --> 00:07:12.959
It's like the commodity that
I see the majority of people

00:07:14.416 --> 00:07:16.849
who aren't getting the places they want

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:19.296
or aren't achieving the things

00:07:19.296 --> 00:07:21.705
that they want in this business

00:07:21.705 --> 00:07:24.325
is strictly based on hustle.

00:07:24.325 --> 00:07:26.501
It's strictly based on being outworked.

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:30.450
It's strictly based on
missing crucial opportunities.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.401
I say all the time, if you stay ready,

00:07:32.401 --> 00:07:33.908
you ain't got to get ready.

00:07:33.908 --> 00:07:37.829
I realized that to have
the level of success

00:07:37.829 --> 00:07:41.253
that I want to have, it's
difficult to spread it out,

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:45.420
and do multiple things, in
order to be world-class.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.824
And I made a decision I
want to be world-class.

00:07:49.824 --> 00:07:53.741
And it takes such a
desperate obsessive focus--

00:07:55.138 --> 00:07:55.971
Yeah.

00:07:55.971 --> 00:07:59.867
- To excel on the level
that I want to make movies.

00:07:59.867 --> 00:08:02.317
You know I was, Star
Wars when I was young.

00:08:02.317 --> 00:08:04.407
I sat in the movie theater
and watched Star Wars,

00:08:04.407 --> 00:08:07.369
and I just couldn't believe
that, that movie made me

00:08:07.369 --> 00:08:10.073
feel like that, just
floored and just stunned

00:08:10.073 --> 00:08:13.648
by the creativity, and just
I'm realizing that in order

00:08:13.648 --> 00:08:16.830
to move people in that way,
in order to touch people

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.781
in that way, you really got to
focus with all of your fiber

00:08:20.781 --> 00:08:23.060
and all of your heart and
all of your creativity.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.682
- A lot of people talk
about talent and they say,

00:08:24.682 --> 00:08:26.174
"Look you are multi-talented

00:08:26.174 --> 00:08:27.708
"and that's why you're a superstar."

00:08:27.708 --> 00:08:30.667
You differentiate though,
between talent and hard work.

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:31.656
- Absolutely.

00:08:31.656 --> 00:08:34.321
- "I've never really viewed
myself as particularly talented.

00:08:34.321 --> 00:08:35.430
"I view myself as, you know,

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.147
"slightly above average in talent.

00:08:37.147 --> 00:08:41.273
"Where I excel is ridiculous,
sickening work ethic.

00:08:41.273 --> 00:08:42.881
"You know, while the other
guys sleeping, I'm working.

00:08:42.881 --> 00:08:44.995
"While the other guys eating, I'm working.

00:08:44.995 --> 00:08:46.202
"While the other guys making love,

00:08:46.202 --> 00:08:48.181
"well I mean, I'm making
love too, but I'm working

00:08:48.181 --> 00:08:49.420
"really hard at it."
- Really hard at it!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.740
- I'm working really hard it!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.802
(laughter)

00:08:51.802 --> 00:08:53.487
- So when the phone rings
and you have an alarm

00:08:53.487 --> 00:08:56.226
goes off say, "Denzel Washington
right now is hookin' up.",

00:08:56.226 --> 00:08:57.822
you got to go at it right now, right.

00:08:57.822 --> 00:08:59.586
(laughter)

00:08:59.586 --> 00:09:03.232
- You know, for me, man,
it's like the separation

00:09:03.232 --> 00:09:06.815
of talent, and skill
is one of the greatest

00:09:07.844 --> 00:09:11.085
misunderstood concepts
for people who are trying

00:09:11.085 --> 00:09:13.233
to excel, who have dreams
that want to do things.

00:09:13.233 --> 00:09:14.580
Talent you have naturally.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.612
Skill is only developed by
hours and hours and hours

00:09:18.612 --> 00:09:20.748
of beatin' on your craft.

00:09:20.748 --> 00:09:24.580
And, you know, for me, I feel
like I have a relationship

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.473
with the audience.

00:09:25.473 --> 00:09:28.587
They agree that they're
going to go in droves,

00:09:28.587 --> 00:09:30.344
and I agree that every time they go,

00:09:30.344 --> 00:09:32.859
it's going to be better
than the last time.

00:09:32.859 --> 00:09:35.323
So I think that's part of the relationship

00:09:35.323 --> 00:09:37.397
and I'm going to hold up my
part as long as they keep

00:09:37.397 --> 00:09:38.334
holdin' up theirs.

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:41.652
The concept of improving
lives runs through the center

00:09:41.652 --> 00:09:45.891
of everything I do, and
then I realized that the way

00:09:45.891 --> 00:09:50.091
to improve lives is to
continually improve yourself.

00:09:50.091 --> 00:09:54.258
So with that, every morning
when I get out of the bed,

00:09:55.445 --> 00:09:59.273
I haven't fixed everything
in the world yet,

00:09:59.273 --> 00:10:01.224
so there's always something to do,

00:10:01.224 --> 00:10:05.284
and in this film, I read
an interesting quote,

00:10:05.284 --> 00:10:08.201
the Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha,

00:10:09.219 --> 00:10:13.302
he said, "That good people
have to get out of the

00:10:14.439 --> 00:10:18.606
"bed everyday and try to
empty the ocean with a ladle."

00:10:20.139 --> 00:10:22.928
Right, and I thought that was, you know,

00:10:22.928 --> 00:10:25.867
I knew that was profound,
and I paused for a second

00:10:25.867 --> 00:10:28.738
and I said alright, "What
the hell is a ladle?"

00:10:28.738 --> 00:10:30.740
(laughter)

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.419
Right, so then I touched it on my iPad,

00:10:33.419 --> 00:10:36.172
it's ladle, oh, it's like a
big spoon, a big spoon, okay.

00:10:36.172 --> 00:10:37.672
A big spoon, yeah!

00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:39.571
A soup spoon.

00:10:39.571 --> 00:10:40.529
I was like why you need a soup spoon?

00:10:40.529 --> 00:10:44.156
So tryin' to empty the
ocean with a soup spoon,

00:10:44.156 --> 00:10:47.418
you know, as the mentality
of how you wake up

00:10:47.418 --> 00:10:50.508
every day to try to do good in the world.

00:10:50.508 --> 00:10:54.091
So for me, I'm really
driven by continually

00:10:55.271 --> 00:10:59.188
trying to elevate my mind
and elevate my spirit

00:11:02.484 --> 00:11:05.815
and care for my body
and to be able to love

00:11:05.815 --> 00:11:09.890
as many people as effectively as possible

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.787
with this mystery of life
that I've been given.

00:11:12.787 --> 00:11:14.087
- Thank guys so much for watching!

00:11:14.087 --> 00:11:15.262
I hope you enjoyed!

00:11:15.262 --> 00:11:17.658
I'd love to know what did
you learn from this video?

00:11:17.658 --> 00:11:19.242
What clips spoke the most to you,

00:11:19.242 --> 00:11:21.648
and how are you going to
apply it immediately somehow

00:11:21.648 --> 00:11:23.209
in your life or in your business?

00:11:23.209 --> 00:11:25.225
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:11:25.225 --> 00:11:26.889
Also if your leaving a
comment, within the first few

00:11:26.889 --> 00:11:28.530
hours of this video going live,

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:31.082
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:11:31.082 --> 00:11:33.439
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Surge Wisdom.

00:11:33.439 --> 00:11:35.394
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:11:35.394 --> 00:11:39.122
You One Word, and doing
multiple reviews on your YouTube

00:11:39.122 --> 00:11:42.184
channel, going chapter
by chapter by chapter.

00:11:42.184 --> 00:11:44.458
I really appreciate the support and I'm so

00:11:44.458 --> 00:11:46.528
glad that you enjoyed my book.

00:11:46.528 --> 00:11:49.111
(upbeat music)

00:11:55.493 --> 00:11:56.384
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:11:56.384 --> 00:11:57.579
I believe in you.

00:11:57.579 --> 00:11:59.609
I hope you'll continue
to believe in yourself

00:11:59.609 --> 00:12:01.701
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:01.701 --> 00:12:03.004
Much love.

00:12:03.004 --> 00:12:04.504
I'll see you soon.

